course: dictionary
lesson: 5531
title: The lee: a sheltered side
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The lee of something is the side that is sheltered from the wind, the side the wind is not blowing onto. Picture a big rock on a windy hill: the side behind it is the lee. «We ate our picnic in the lee of the big rock, out of the wind.» The rock blocks the wind, so the lee is calm.
explain: On a boat, the lee side is the side away from the wind, and sailors also call this direction leeward. The side the wind hits first is the windward side. If you can say which side the wind is coming from, you can work out which side is the lee.
explain: Lee with a capital letter is different. It is a name, like Lee or Tim Berners-Lee. «Tim Berners-Lee invented the World Wide Web in 1989.» Here there is no wind at all. The capital letter and the person in the sentence tell you it is a name.
fact: The lee is the side sheltered from the wind.
fact: Leeward means the same as lee: the side away from the wind.
fact: «In the lee of» means sheltered by something, such as a wall, a rock or a hedge.
fact: Rain falls on the windward side of a mountain first, so the lee side is often drier. This is called a rain shadow.
fact: Lee with a capital letter is a name, as in «Tim Berners-Lee invented the World Wide Web in 1989.»
exercise: «We sheltered in the lee of the big rock.» What does lee mean here? | A loud noise | The side the wind hits first | A deep, wet puddle | *The side sheltered from the wind
exercise: On a sailing boat, which side is the lee side? | *The side away from the wind | The front of the boat | The side with the anchor | The side the wind is blowing onto
exercise: «Tim Berners-Lee invented the World Wide Web in 1989.» Why is Lee written with a capital letter? | *It is part of a person's name | It means a sheltered side | It starts a new sentence in the middle | It is the name of a wind
test: Which word means the side away from the wind? | *Leeward | Gusty | Windward | Stormy
test: Rain falls first on the windward side of a mountain. Which side is drier? | The very top only | The windward side | Both sides are the same | *The lee side
exam: Tim said, «Priya-Lee needs to get out, and the door is on Shanaya's side.» What is Lee in Priya-Lee? | A kind of boat | *A part of a name, not a sheltered side | A strong wind | The sheltered side of a door
